tonin darkens skin" — clean, easy, but **doesn't match observed evidence** (no correlation between melatonin levels and baseline skin tone across individuals/populations) - **More detailed explanation:** melanocyte/tyrosinase/melanin pathway — more steps, but **matches all observed evidence**, including why albinism happens, why sun exposure darkens skin, why populations evolved different baseline tones, etc. Between an elegant story that doesn't fit the facts and a more detailed story that does fit the facts, the detailed-but-accurate one has to win — that's just how evidence works, even when the simpler story is more appealing intuitively.
